https://github.com/AbuZar-Ansarii/PrivateAgent # Only manifest provider boilerplate; no Shizuku source usage (dep hits, zero UserService).
https://github.com/TensorHub-ORG/Storydex # Desktop-first AI novel workbench; Android Shizuku limited to an optional self-check/permission helper.
https://github.com/Zheke32174/understory-passgen # Hardened password manager whose Shizuku/Dhizuku elevation tier is stubbed/deferred; suite targets public APIs only.
https://github.com/Crescent-of-Maya/MndroLua # No functional Shizuku calls; only manifest boilerplate and template, README never mentions Shizuku.
https://github.com/kabzon93region/Quest-Task-Manager-Standalone # Standalone build explicitly removes Shizuku (v2.1.1+); uses Wireless ADB instead, Russian-only README.
https://github.com/Horizon-25/SmartSwap # ShizukuHelper does ping/permission only (code comment: shell-exec removed); app-data-via-Shizuku unimplemented; offline transfer works without it.
https://github.com/abdellatif-laghjaj/ClipSave # Shizuku integration is status display only; downloads need neither Shizuku nor root.
https://github.com/gufei233/KJQ-TOKEN-ADB # LADB fork (draco package, LADB BSD license); Shizuku only probed for incompatibility warning, README says uninstall Shizuku to use LADB.
https://github.com/Zheke32174/understory-backups # Understory suite targets public APIs only (no-Shizuku design constraint); Shizuku lives in an optional elevation broker, app is alpha with no license.
https://github.com/xishanp/doroUbuntu # Shizuku limited to a permission-status page; proot-Ubuntu core uses no privileged operations.

